schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: "Which Chain Is Right for Your Project?"
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: comparison
  summary: >-
    A decision-framework guide (Somaliland/East Africa audience, Community-
    Steward level) for choosing a blockchain among 1,000+ options. Frames the
    choice around the "blockchain trilemma" (scalability, security,
    decentralization), maps use cases to chains (Ethereum L1 for high-value
    DeFi, Layer 2s like Base/Optimism/Arbitrum for general apps, Solana for
    high-volume consumer apps, Polygon for gaming), gives a TPS/fee comparison
    table, covers ecosystem/composability, developer-language fit (Solidity vs
    Rust vs Move), EVM-compatibility, consensus-mechanism energy tradeoffs
    (PoS vs PoW), and cross-chain bridge risk, closing with a six-question
    decision framework.
  audience: community-steward-level project builders choosing a blockchain
  known_tensions:
    - >-
      The blockchain trilemma itself — the article states plainly that
      optimizing for one of scalability/security/decentralization typically
      means compromising on another; there is no chain that maximizes all
      three.
  related_concepts:
    - blockchain-trilemma
  related_resources:
    - l2beat
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/which-chain-right.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted

# assessed-but-excluded:
# - The TPS/fee comparison table (Ethereum L1, Base, Arbitrum, Solana, Polygon) is captured as
#   a single claim-evidence entry with an explicit currency/uncertainty caveat rather than five
#   separate resource cards, since the numbers themselves (not the chains as distinct projects)
#   are the load-bearing content and are highly time-sensitive.
# - Did not create individual resource cards for Polkadot/Cosmos/Aptos/Sui — mentioned only in
#   passing as language/interoperability examples, not developed as named subjects.
